<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>1</b></sup> Unto thee, O LORD, do I lift up my soul.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>2</b></sup> O my God, I trust in thee: let me not be ashamed, let not mine enemies triumph over me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>3</b></sup> Yea, let none that wait on thee be ashamed: let them be ashamed which transgress without cause.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>4</b></sup> Shew me thy ways, O LORD; teach me thy paths.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>5</b></sup> Lead me in thy truth, and teach me: for thou <i>art</i> the God of my salvation; on thee do I wait all the day.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>6</b></sup> Remember, O LORD, thy tender mercies and thy lovingkindnesses; for they <i>have been</i> ever of old.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>7</b></sup> Remember not the sins of my youth, nor my transgressions: according to thy mercy remember thou me for thy goodness’ sake, O LORD.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>8</b></sup> Good and upright <i>is</i> the LORD: therefore will he teach sinners in the way.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>9</b></sup> The meek will he guide in judgment: and the meek will he teach his way.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>10</b></sup> All the paths of the LORD <i>are</i> mercy and truth unto such as keep his covenant and his testimonies.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>11</b></sup> For thy name’s sake, O LORD, pardon mine iniquity; for it <i>is</i> great.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>12</b></sup> What man <i>is</i> he that feareth the LORD? him shall he teach in the way <i>that</i> he shall choose.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>13</b></sup> His soul shall dwell at ease; and his seed shall inherit the earth.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>14</b></sup> The secret of the LORD <i>is</i> with them that fear him; and he will shew them his covenant.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>15</b></sup> Mine eyes <i>are</i> ever toward the LORD; for he shall pluck my feet out of the net.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>16</b></sup> Turn thee unto me, and have mercy upon me; for I <i>am</i> desolate and afflicted.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>17</b></sup> The troubles of my heart are enlarged: <i>O</i> bring thou me out of my distresses.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>18</b></sup> Look upon mine affliction and my pain; and forgive all my sins.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>19</b></sup> Consider mine enemies; for they are many; and they hate me with cruel hatred.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>20</b></sup> O keep my soul, and deliver me: let me not be ashamed; for I put my trust in thee.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>21</b></sup> Let integrity and uprightness preserve me; for I wait on thee.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm"><i>A Psalm</i> of David.</title><sup><b>22</b></sup> Redeem Israel, O God, out of all his troubles. <br />
